-- החלטת ועדת מעקב מיום 14.1.2025 — טעויות סופר ותיקונים להסכם השכר מיום
-- 19.10.2022: the follow-up committee of the wage agreement, deciding under
-- its §35, mends what fell by oversight into several clauses and annexes,
-- and records that the teachers were paid as the parties had agreed. (1)–(2)
-- a teacher placed in the tables on the day they change — an existing one
-- moving to the reform on 1.9.2022, one moving to a principal's or first
-- deputy's post on 1.9.2022 or 1.9.2023 — is placed as if they changed a day
-- later, first in the old tables and then updated; (3) the BA and MA tables
-- and their Ofek supplements (א1, א2, ב1, ב2, ג1, ג2), printed to the
-- shekel, give way to tables printed to the agora; (4) the principals'
-- tables (א8, א9) give way to tables א'8 and א'9, which add the
-- non-academic managers; (5) annex ג3 applies from 1.9.23, not 1.1.23;
-- (6) §6 applies to first deputies too, with §99 for §72; (7) the vacation
-- days of §29 are divided by sector — 29.1.2–29.1.3 for the Jewish and
-- Druze sectors, a new 29.1.3א for the Arab sector, whose spring vacation
-- was shortened.
--
-- It amends the agreement of 19.10.2022, so it imports the agreement's
-- module and its signed copy's (whose annexes it replaces), and writes only
-- what it changes, dated. Three of the agreement's findings are the flaws
-- it cures: F-ofek-hadash-wage-2022-b (§6 names no first deputy),
-- F-ofek-hadash-wage-2022-signed-a (ג3's day), -signed-b (the tables to the
-- shekel) and -signed-c (no non-academic managers' table); they are
-- referenced here, not filed again. Its tables א1, א2, ב1, ב2, ג1 and ג2
-- are data, cell for cell; the corpus publishes them as (grade, seniority,
-- amount) triples, written here in the signed copy's shape, a row per
-- seniority. Annexes א'8 and א'9 (pages 6–13 of the decision) are not in
-- the corpus: a named input.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `2022-10-19_ofek-hadash_wage-agreement_signed-appendices`

§ `החלטת ועדת המעקב מיום 14.1.2025 — טעויות סופר וטבלאות שכר ברמת אגורות`

-- akn:preamble The decision's frame: a label row with no text of its own.
-- akn:preamble/p1 A file number written in by hand (2025-323); no rule.
-- akn:preamble/p2 The registration stamp under the Collective Agreements Law, its date and number not legible; no rule.
-- akn:preamble/p3 A stamp "this collective agreement was registered"; no rule.
-- akn:preamble/p4 The agreement number (20250135); no rule.
-- akn:preamble/p5 A "true to the original" stamp; no rule.

-- The day of the decision, written in by hand; the committee of §35 of the
-- agreement of 19.10.2022 met that day and decided as follows, finally and
-- bindingly (§35, imported).
@ref akn:preamble/p6 akn:preamble/p7
`the decision of 14.1.2025 was taken on` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 14 1 2025

#ASSERT `what binds the parties in a dispute` "the decision of 14.1.2025" "a party's other reading" EQUALS "the decision of 14.1.2025"

-- The recitals: errors fell by oversight into several clauses and annexes
-- of the agreement; and the teachers were in fact paid as the parties had
-- agreed, as the decision details. So what the decision corrects it
-- corrects from the day the agreement set, not from 14.1.2025.
@ref akn:preamble/p8 akn:preamble/p9
`the decision of 14.1.2025 corrects from the agreement's own days` MEANS TRUE

-- akn:preamble/p10 The words that introduce the decision's clauses; no rule.

§§ `1–2 מועד עדכון הטבלאות לצורך שיבוץ`

DECLARE `placement on the day the tables change` IS ONE OF
    `an existing teacher moving to the reform's terms on 1.9.2022`
    `moving to a principal's or first deputy's post on 1.9.2022`
    `moving to a principal's or first deputy's post on 1.9.2023`
    `another placement`

-- 1: notwithstanding §4.1, for placing in the tables in 1.א — an existing
-- teaching employee (as the reform agreement of 25.12.2008, as amended,
-- means one) who moves to the reform's terms on 1.9.2022 and is placed by
-- §47 of it — and 1.ב — one who moves to a principal's or first deputy's
-- post on 1.9.2022 and is placed in their tables — the tables are deemed
-- updated on 2.9.2022: first the placement in the tables before §4.1
-- updates them, then the update. 2: notwithstanding §4.2, the same for one
-- who moves to a principal's or first deputy's post on 1.9.2023, the
-- tables deemed updated on 2.9.2023.
@ref akn:art_1 akn:art_1__para_a akn:art_1__para_b akn:art_2
GIVEN p IS A `placement on the day the tables change`
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `the day the tables are deemed updated for the placement` p IS
    CONSIDER p
    WHEN `an existing teacher moving to the reform's terms on 1.9.2022` THEN JUST (DATE_FROM_DMY 2 9 2022)
    WHEN `moving to a principal's or first deputy's post on 1.9.2022` THEN JUST (DATE_FROM_DMY 2 9 2022)
    WHEN `moving to a principal's or first deputy's post on 1.9.2023` THEN JUST (DATE_FROM_DMY 2 9 2023)
    WHEN `another placement` THEN NOTHING

-- The two steps, in the agreement's own rule (`the combined-salary table in
-- force`, imported): the placement is made in the table in force before the
-- change (on 31 August, as the deeming keeps 1 September in the old
-- tables), and the table in force on the deemed day follows it. Another
-- placement is made in the table in force on its day.
GIVEN p IS A `placement on the day the tables change`
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `the last day of the old tables for the placement` p IS
    CONSIDER p
    WHEN `an existing teacher moving to the reform's terms on 1.9.2022` THEN JUST (DATE_FROM_DMY 31 8 2022)
    WHEN `moving to a principal's or first deputy's post on 1.9.2022` THEN JUST (DATE_FROM_DMY 31 8 2022)
    WHEN `moving to a principal's or first deputy's post on 1.9.2023` THEN JUST (DATE_FROM_DMY 31 8 2023)
    WHEN `another placement` THEN NOTHING

GIVEN p IS A `placement on the day the tables change`, n IS A NUMBER, `the day of the placement` IS A DATE
GIVETH A LIST OF `combined-salary table`
DECIDE `the tables a placement goes through` p n `the day of the placement` IS
    CONSIDER `the last day of the old tables for the placement` p
    WHEN JUST old THEN LIST `the combined-salary table in force` n old, `the combined-salary table in force` n (`the deemed day` p)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN LIST `the combined-salary table in force` n `the day of the placement`
    WHERE
        GIVEN q IS A `placement on the day the tables change`
        GIVETH A DATE
        DECIDE `the deemed day` q IS
            CONSIDER `the day the tables are deemed updated for the placement` q
            WHEN JUST d THEN d
            WHEN NOTHING THEN `the day of the placement`

#ASSERT (    `the tables a placement goes through` `an existing teacher moving to the reform's terms on 1.9.2022` 3 (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 9 2022)
         EQUALS LIST `the table in force on the eve of the signing`, `annex א` 3)
#ASSERT (    `the tables a placement goes through` `moving to a principal's or first deputy's post on 1.9.2023` 8 (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 9 2023)
         EQUALS LIST `annex א` 8, `annex א` 9)
-- Without the decision, a placement on 1.9.2022 is straight into the new
-- table.
#ASSERT `the tables a placement goes through` `another placement` 3 (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 9 2022) EQUALS LIST `annex א` 3

§§ `3 טבלאות שכר ברמת אגורות`

-- 3: the tables rounded to the shekel annexed to the agreement as א1, א2,
-- ב1, ב2, ג1 and ג2 give way to tables rounded to the agora, annexed to the
-- decision under the same labels (below); the agorot were left out by
-- oversight. This is the flaw F-ofek-hadash-wage-2022-signed-b records in
-- the signed copy. The other annexes stand.
@ref akn:art_3
GIVEN a IS A `signed-copy annex`
GIVETH A `signed-copy annex`
DECIDE `the annex as the decision of 14.1.2025 has it` a IS
    CONSIDER filter (GIVEN b YIELD b's `signed-copy annex label` EQUALS a's `signed-copy annex label`) `the decision's agora annexes`
    WHEN b FOLLOWED BY rest THEN b
    WHEN EMPTY THEN a

-- The agreement's §4 table salary, read on the corrected annexes.
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER, d IS A DATE, i IS A NUMBER, label IS A NUMBER, grade IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `the table salary under §4 as the decision of 14.1.2025 corrects it` n d i label grade IS
    CONSIDER `the combined-salary table in force` n d
    WHEN `annex א` k THEN `the signed-copy cell` (`the table numbered` i `in` (`the annex as the decision of 14.1.2025 has it` (at `the signed copy's combined-salary annexes` (k MINUS 1)))) label grade
    WHEN `the table in force on the eve of the signing` THEN NOTHING

-- The agreement's §5 supplement, read on the corrected annexes.
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER, d IS A DATE, grade IS A NUMBER, `position share` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `the Ofek 2022 supplement as the decision of 14.1.2025 corrects it` n d grade `position share` IS
    CONSIDER `the Ofek 2022 annexes in force` d
    WHEN `annexes ב1 to ב7` THEN `the supplement from` (`the annex as the decision of 14.1.2025 has it` (at `the signed copy's annexes ב` (n MINUS 1)))
    WHEN `annexes ג1 to ג7` THEN `the supplement from` (`the annex as the decision of 14.1.2025 has it` (at `the signed copy's annexes ג` (n MINUS 1)))
    WHEN `no Ofek 2022 supplement` THEN JUST 0
    WHERE
        GIVEN a IS A `signed-copy annex`
        GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
        DECIDE `the supplement from` a IS
            CONSIDER `the signed-copy cell` (`the table numbered` 1 `in` a) 0 grade
            WHEN JUST amount THEN JUST (`the Ofek 2022 supplement` amount `position share`)
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

-- A BA teacher at grade 1 and seniority 3: 6,555 by the signed copy's א1,
-- 6,554.52 by the decision's.
#ASSERT `the table salary under §4 on` 1 (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 9 2022) 1 3 1 EQUALS JUST 6555
#ASSERT `the table salary under §4 as the decision of 14.1.2025 corrects it` 1 (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 9 2022) 1 3 1 EQUALS JUST 6554.52
#ASSERT `the Ofek 2022 supplement as the decision of 14.1.2025 corrects it` 2 (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 9 2023) 1 1 EQUALS JUST 1664.87
-- An annex the decision does not replace reads as the signed copy prints it.
#ASSERT `the table salary under §4 as the decision of 14.1.2025 corrects it` 3 (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 9 2022) 1 3 1.5 EQUALS `the table salary under §4 on` 3 (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 9 2022) 1 3 1.5

§§ `4 טבלאות המנהלים א'8 ו־א'9`

-- 4: annexes א8 and א9 give way to tables א'8 and א'9 annexed to the
-- decision, for principals, first deputies and junior-high principals in a
-- six-year school who are not academics, as the case may be; tables were
-- left out of them by oversight (F-ofek-hadash-wage-2022-signed-c). The
-- decision's pages that print א'8 and א'9 are not in the corpus, so each is
-- a named input.
@ref akn:art_4
ASSUME `annex א'8 of the decision of 14.1.2025` IS A `signed-copy annex`
@ref akn:art_4
ASSUME `annex א'9 of the decision of 14.1.2025` IS A `signed-copy annex`

-- The principals' annex a placement under §4 reads after the decision:
-- א'8 for א8's place, א'9 for א9's.
DECLARE `principals' annex after the decision of 14.1.2025` IS ONE OF
    `annex א'8 of the decision`
    `annex א'9 of the decision`

GIVEN k IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE `principals' annex after the decision of 14.1.2025`
DECIDE `the principals' annex in place of annex א` k IS
    BRANCH IF k EQUALS 8 THEN JUST `annex א'8 of the decision`
           IF k EQUALS 9 THEN JUST `annex א'9 of the decision`
           OTHERWISE NOTHING

#ASSERT `the principals' annex in place of annex א` 9 EQUALS JUST `annex א'9 of the decision`
#ASSERT `the principals' annex in place of annex א` 3 EQUALS NOTHING

-- akn:art_4/p2 Hand-written numbers (1, 2, 3) on the page; no rule.
-- akn:art_4/p3 The signatures on the first page; no rule.
-- akn:art_4/p4 A "true to the original" stamp; no rule.

§§ `5 מועד החלת נספח ג'3`

-- 5: by §5.2 of the agreement, annex ג3, "the Ofek 2022 supplement for
-- BA teachers (rating code 101)", applies from 1.9.23; "1.1.23" printed in
-- it is a scribal error (F-ofek-hadash-wage-2022-signed-a). The day is the
-- one the agreement's §5.2 sets, which the signed copy's encoding already
-- applies.
@ref akn:art_5
`the day annex ג3 applies from, as the decision of 14.1.2025 says` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 1 9 2023

#ASSERT `the day annex ג3 applies from, as the decision of 14.1.2025 says` EQUALS `the day §§4–5 apply the annex from` `annex ג3 of the signed copy`
#ASSERT NOT (`the day annex ג3 applies from, as the decision of 14.1.2025 says` EQUALS `the day the annex prints` `annex ג3 of the signed copy`)

§§ `6 תוספת אישית לסגנים ראשונים`

-- 6: as agreed in the agreement, its §6 applies to first deputies too,
-- with the changes called for: for them "§99" in place of "§72"; first
-- deputies were left out of §6 by oversight. This cures the gap
-- F-ofek-hadash-wage-2022-b records (`§6 names no first deputy`, imported),
-- from the agreement's own days (the recital).
@ref akn:art_6
GIVEN m IS A `manager with a personal supplement`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `§6 updates the personal supplement of, as the decision of 14.1.2025 has it` m IF
    TRUE

GIVEN m IS A `manager with a personal supplement`
GIVETH A STRING
DECIDE `the section whose method §6's C replaces for` m IS
    CONSIDER m
    WHEN `a principal entitled under §72` THEN "72"
    WHEN `a first deputy entitled under §99` THEN "99"

#ASSERT `§6 updates the personal supplement of, as the decision of 14.1.2025 has it` `a first deputy entitled under §99`
#ASSERT NOT `§6 updates the personal supplement of` `a first deputy entitled under §99`
-- The first deputy's rate by §6's formula: 2,000 kept on a new table salary
-- of 16,000 is 12.5%.
#ASSERT `the updated personal supplement rate` 2000 16000 EQUALS 12.5%

§§ `7 ימי חופשה`

-- akn:art_7 The clause's heading, "vacation days"; its amendments are (א)–(ג).
-- akn:art_7/p1 The lead-in: §29 of the agreement is amended as follows.

DECLARE `sector of 14.1.2025` IS ONE OF
    `the Jewish sector`
    `the Druze sector`
    `the Arab sector`

@desc A teaching employee, as far as §29 as the decision of 14.1.2025 amends it asks.
DECLARE `sector vacation-day teacher` HAS
    `as §29 asks`                                      IS A `vacation-day teacher`
    `the teacher's sector`                             IS A `sector of 14.1.2025`
    `the sector of the institutions he is placed in`   IS A `sector of 14.1.2025`
    `days of the shortened spring vacation he must work` IS A NUMBER @desc by the placement and system hours, not as a substitute

-- F-ofek-hadash-maakav-2025-a: (א) gives 29.1.2–29.1.3 to "a teaching
-- employee from the Jewish or Druze sector", and (ב) 29.1.3א to "a teaching
-- employee from the Arab sector placed ... in institutions of the Arab
-- sector". A teacher from the Arab sector placed in a Jewish-sector school
-- is in neither, if "from the sector" is the teacher's own. The sector is
-- read as the sector of the institutions he is placed in (convention
-- reading.consistent: every teacher placed for part of the year has one of
-- the rules), so he has 29.1.2–29.1.3.
GIVEN t IS A `sector vacation-day teacher`
GIVETH A `sector of 14.1.2025`
DECIDE `the sector §29 reads for` t IS
    t's `the sector of the institutions he is placed in`

-- (א): in 29.1.2 and 29.1.3, "a teaching employee" becomes "a teaching
-- employee from the Jewish or the Druze sector". (ב): after 29.1.3,
-- 29.1.3א: a teaching employee from the Arab sector placed for less than a
-- full school year in institutions of the Arab sector who, by the placement
-- and the system hours, must work on one day of the (shortened) spring
-- vacation has one vacation day, and on two days, two; the vacation days in
-- a school year are never more than 29.1.1's two. 29.1.1 (a full school
-- year, two days) is unchanged.
@ref akn:art_7__para_a akn:art_7__para_b
GIVEN t IS A `sector vacation-day teacher`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the vacation days for the school year, as the decision of 14.1.2025 amends §29` t IS
    IF t's `as §29 asks`'s `placed for a full school year`
    THEN `the vacation days for the school year` (t's `as §29 asks`)
    ELSE (IF `the sector §29 reads for` t EQUALS `the Arab sector`
          THEN min (t's `days of the shortened spring vacation he must work`) 2
          ELSE `the vacation days for the school year` (t's `as §29 asks`))

-- The other reading: the teacher's own sector.
GIVEN t IS A `sector vacation-day teacher`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the vacation days by the teacher's own sector` t IS
    IF t's `as §29 asks`'s `placed for a full school year`
    THEN `the vacation days for the school year` (t's `as §29 asks`)
    ELSE (IF t's `the teacher's sector` EQUALS `the Arab sector`
          THEN (IF t's `the sector of the institutions he is placed in` EQUALS `the Arab sector`
                THEN min (t's `days of the shortened spring vacation he must work`) 2
                ELSE 0)
          ELSE `the vacation days for the school year` (t's `as §29 asks`))

GIVEN own IS A `sector of 14.1.2025`, placed IS A `sector of 14.1.2025`, spring IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `sector vacation-day teacher`
DECIDE `a part-year teacher of` own `placed in` placed `working spring days` spring IS
    `sector vacation-day teacher` WITH
        `as §29 asks` IS `vacation-day teacher` WITH
                             `placed for a full school year`  IS FALSE
                             `placed in a full position`      IS FALSE
                             `must work on 13 Adar or the first day of the winter vacation` IS TRUE
                             `must work on 18 Iyar or the first day of the spring vacation` IS TRUE
        `the teacher's sector`                             IS own
        `the sector of the institutions he is placed in`   IS placed
        `days of the shortened spring vacation he must work` IS spring

#ASSERT `the vacation days for the school year, as the decision of 14.1.2025 amends §29` (`a part-year teacher of` `the Arab sector` `placed in` `the Arab sector` `working spring days` 1) EQUALS 1
#ASSERT `the vacation days for the school year, as the decision of 14.1.2025 amends §29` (`a part-year teacher of` `the Arab sector` `placed in` `the Arab sector` `working spring days` 3) EQUALS 2
#ASSERT `the vacation days for the school year, as the decision of 14.1.2025 amends §29` (`a part-year teacher of` `the Druze sector` `placed in` `the Druze sector` `working spring days` 0) EQUALS 2

`an Arab-sector teacher placed in a Jewish-sector school has days by the reading and none by his own sector` MEANS
        `the vacation days for the school year, as the decision of 14.1.2025 amends §29` (`a part-year teacher of` `the Arab sector` `placed in` `the Jewish sector` `working spring days` 0) EQUALS 2
    AND `the vacation days by the teacher's own sector` (`a part-year teacher of` `the Arab sector` `placed in` `the Jewish sector` `working spring days` 0) EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `an Arab-sector teacher placed in a Jewish-sector school has days by the reading and none by his own sector`

-- (ג): in 29.1.4, after "as in 29.1.2 and 29.1.3" comes "and 29.1.3א": the
-- day is taken in that school year, and only after the days named are
-- worked (the agreement's rule, imported).
@ref akn:art_7__para_c
GIVEN `worked the date` IS A BOOLEAN, `in maternity or reserve duty on the date` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `may take the day 29.1.3א gives` `worked the date` `in maternity or reserve duty on the date` IF
    `may take the day earned by the date` `worked the date` `in maternity or reserve duty on the date`

DECLARE `registration action of 14.1.2025` IS ONE OF
    `submit the decision of 14.1.2025 for registration and attach it to the agreement`

-- 8: the decision is submitted for registration and attached to the
-- agreement. No day is set (convention dates.no-deadline).
@ref akn:art_8
`registering the decision of 14.1.2025` MEANS
    PARTY `the follow-up committee`
    MUST  `submit the decision of 14.1.2025 for registration and attach it to the agreement`

-- akn:conclusions The sign-off: a label row with no text of its own.
-- akn:conclusions/p1 The signatures; no rule.
-- akn:conclusions/p2 The wages commissioner's post; no rule.
-- akn:conclusions/p3 The Director-General's post; no rule.
-- akn:conclusions/p4 The union's secretary-general's post; no rule.

§§ `נספחים א1, א2, ב1, ב2, ג1 ו־ג2 — טבלאות ברמת אגורות`

